# Code follows ARCHITECTURE.md

`ARCHITECTURE.md` at the repo root is the single source of truth for the project structure: the module map, the layer rules, and the migration table. A file that does not fit one of the modules in the map is misplaced — extend the map first.

## Where things live

- The module map in `ARCHITECTURE.md` decides placement and naming. Every module file carries the full dotted prefix (`pware.oc.<layer>.<name>`); barrels are `index.ts`.
- A new module goes into the layer the map says. A moved or renamed module changes its name and imports in the same turn.
- `test/` mirrors `src/` one file per module.

## Layer rules

| Layer | May import |
| --- | --- |
| `pware.oc.ui` | anything below |
| `pware.oc.perf` | core + ui (view) |
| `pware.oc.runtime` | opencode, omo, core |
| `pware.oc.opencode` | core |
| `pware.oc.omo` | opencode, core |
| `pware.oc.core` | nothing |

- `core` never imports a domain or the UI.
- OpenCode is the required host: `opencode` owns generic SQLite reads and host events.
- OMO is an optional OpenCode plugin integration: `omo` owns OMO-specific artifacts and may read `opencode` data to correlate them with host sessions, parts, todos, or events.
- The dependency is one-way: `opencode` never imports OMO or interprets `.omo/` / `.sisyphus/` artifacts.
- `runtime` composes the always-present OpenCode snapshot with optional OMO-aware capabilities.
- Keep the import graph acyclic. A file that needs a dependency from a higher layer moves up a layer instead of importing down.

## Keep the map honest

- After any `src/` move, rename, or new module, update `ARCHITECTURE.md` in the same turn.
- After a public export documented in the map is renamed, update the map's "Key exports".

## Do not

- Create a file that does not fit the module map — extend the map first.
- Duplicate the module map in another doc (README, backlog) — `ARCHITECTURE.md` is the one.
- Import upward: a `pware.oc.core` file importing `pware.oc.ui` or a domain is a bug.
- Duplicate the "update docs in the same turn" rule — that is `docs-sync.mdc`.
